laurel 2404: TopazModem.cpp is shared with TopazAudio (ADSP loader, area F): (1) every TrustZone call (scm(), topaz_scm(), the hyp_assign of MSA/rmtfs) runs under one lock over the whole call incl. the resume loop (x0 = 1, session in x6); a busy answer (SCM_V2_EBUSY -12) is retried after 30 ms, at most 100 times, the lock released while waiting (qcom_scm / downstream scm.c behaviour); the modem PAS and the ADSP PAS run in parallel threads at boot. (2) smmu_identity()/topaz_smmu_identity(): one lock over the read of the SMRs/S2CRs, the pick of a free SMR and context bank and the writes (WLAN stream 0x80 and the audio stream raced for the same slot); the SMMU is mapped once. (3) topaz_soc_map checks that the modem pool [MODEM_POOL_BASE, +SIZE) lies outside XNU's RAM [gPhysBase, gPhysBase + gPhysSize); on overlap one line 'LAUREL MODEM POOL: off: modem pool .. overlaps XNU RAM ..: modem, Wi-Fi and ADSP audio off' and topaz_soc_map fails (modem thread and TopazAudio stop; the LAUREL WIFI line names the reason). Area A map (uefi-boot.md): pool 0xE0000000-0xE1000000, XNU 0xE1004000-0x1AD004000: no overlap.

